# Everything here is excluded from the build context — the tarball Docker
# sends to the daemon before building. A fat context makes every build slow
# even when nothing changed, and anything sent can accidentally end up in the
# image via a careless COPY.

# Verification and experiment scripts: useful in the repo, dead weight in
# the container. The service needs main.py, pipeline.py, obb_postprocess.py.
export_onnx.py
verify_stage1.py
verify_obb.py
verify_pipeline.py
bench_detector.py
diagnose_obb_gap.py
preprocessing_experiment.py
preprocessing_experiment2.py
find_dataset.py

# Windows helper scripts
*.bat

# Reports and generated JSON
models/*.json
!models/classifier_meta.json

# Never ship credentials. The Dockerfile does not COPY them, but defence in
# depth: if they are not in the context, a future careless `COPY . .` cannot
# pick them up either.
*.env
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*credentials*
*service-account*
gcp-key*.json

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Git and IDE
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

# Docs
*.md
